StashVent shares unfinished Git work. A stash is packaged, encrypted on this
machine with a password, and uploaded. Whoever has the link and the password
can import it into their own stash list. The server never sees the password
or the contents.

Usage:
  stashvent <command> [flags]

Examples:
  # Share the newest stash; prints a link and a password
  stashvent push

  # Import a shared stash (asks for the password)
  stashvent pull https://stashvent.example/8xK29qLm4Tz7

  # See what this machine has shared, and take a share back
  stashvent list
  stashvent delete 8xK29qLm4Tz7

Commands:
  delete      Delete a share from the server before it expires
  help        Help about any command
  list        List the shares sent from this machine
  login       Save the API key you were given for a server
  logout      Remove the saved API key for a server
  pull        Download, decrypt, and import a shared stash
  push        Encrypt and share a stash
  version     Print the stashvent version and commit

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for stashvent
      --server string   StashVent server URL (env STASHVENT_SERVER)
  -v, --version         version for stashvent

Use "stashvent <command> --help" for more information about a command.
